

HOSTS(5)             UNIX Programmer's Manual             HOSTS(5)



NAME
     hosts - static host name database

DESCRIPTION
     The file /etc/hosts maps host names to Internet addresses; it
     is consulted by gethostbyname(3) before DNS.  Each line gives
     one address followed by one or more names for it:

          a.b.c.d   official-name   [alias ...]

     Fields are separated by spaces or tabs.  Blank lines and text
     from a `#' to the end of line are ignored.  For example:

          127.0.0.1     localhost
          192.168.2.1   gateway gw router

     A reverse lookup (address to name) returns the first name on
     the matching line.

FILES
     /etc/hosts

SEE ALSO
     host(1), gethostbyname(3), resolv.conf(5)



